Four-term Democrat [[Tom Carper]] was [[2018 United States Senate election in Delaware|reelected in 2018]] with 60.0% of the vote. He announced on May 22, 2023, that he will be retiring, and will not run for a fifth term.<ref name=":2">{{Cite web |last=Robertson |first=Nicky |date=2023-05-22 |title=Longtime Democratic Sen. Tom Carper says he will not seek reelection |url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/05/22/politics/tom-carper-reelection/index.html |access-date=2023-05-22 |website=CNN Politics |publisher=[[CNN]] |language=en |archive-date=May 22, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230522165517/https://www.cnn.com/2023/05/22/politics/tom-carper-reelection/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

Delaware's at-large U.S. representative [[Lisa Blunt Rochester]] is running for the Democratic nomination to succeed Carper, who endorsed her when he announced his retirement.<ref name="Politico-June-1">{{cite web |last1=Mutnick |first1=Ally |last2=Otterbein |first2=Holly |title=Rep. Lisa Blunt Rochester to launch run for Delaware Senate seat in June |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2023/06/01/lisa-blunt-rochester-delaware-senate-seat-00099778 |website=[[Politico]] |language=en |date=June 1, 2023 |access-date=June 7, 2023 |archive-date=June 8, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230608214450/https://www.politico.com/news/2023/06/01/lisa-blunt-rochester-delaware-senate-seat-00099778 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=LBR>{{Cite web |last=Mizelle |first=Shawna |date=2023-06-21 |title=Rep. Lisa Blunt Rochester announces Senate bid in Delaware |url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/06/21/politics/lisa-blunt-rochester-senate-delaware/index.html |access-date=2023-06-21 |website=CNN |language=en |archive-date=June 21, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230621124157/https://www.cnn.com/2023/06/21/politics/lisa-blunt-rochester-senate-delaware/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

Term-limited [[Governor of Delaware|governor]] [[John Carney (Delaware politician)|John Carney]] was also considered a possible Democratic candidate.<ref name=":2" /><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.politico.com/news/2023/02/03/maryland-dems-cardin-reelection-00081005|title=Old Bay melee: Maryland Dems circle as Cardin weighs reelection|website=[[Politico]]|date=February 3, 2023|access-date=February 28, 2023|archive-date=February 28, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230228074236/https://www.politico.com/news/2023/02/03/maryland-dems-cardin-reelection-00081005|url-status=live}}</ref> Carney announced that he is running for mayor of [[Wilmington, Delaware|Wilmington]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.delawareonline.com/story/news/local/2023/10/04/wilmington-mayor-mike-purzycki-wont-run-for-re-election-2024/71060994007/ | title=Carney expresses interest in Wilmington mayor after Purzycki announces he won't run in 2024 | access-date=October 5, 2023 | archive-date=October 5, 2023 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231005185433/https://www.delawareonline.com/story/news/local/2023/10/04/wilmington-mayor-mike-purzycki-wont-run-for-re-election-2024/71060994007/ | url-status=live }}</ref>

