Two-term Republican [[Roger Wicker]] was [[2018 United States Senate election in Mississippi|reelected in 2018]] with 58.5% of the vote. Wicker is running for a third full term. He faced a primary challenge from conservative [[Mississippi House of Representatives|state representative]] [[Dan Eubanks]] and won by a comfortable margin.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Corder |first=Frank |date=2023-06-19 |title=Senate 2024: Eubanks files to challenge Wicker |url=https://magnoliatribune.com/2023/06/19/senate-2024-eubanks-files-to-challenge-wicker/ |access-date=2023-07-01 |website=Magnolia Tribune |language=en-US |archive-date=June 20, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230620211521/https://magnoliatribune.com/2023/06/19/senate-2024-eubanks-files-to-challenge-wicker/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Wicker will face Democratic lawyer Ty Pinkins in the general election.<ref name=Ty>{{Cite web|last=Vance|first=Taylor|date=January 4, 2023|title=Army veteran Ty Pinkins announces campaign against US Sen. Roger Wicker|quote=Phillip Waller, the communications director for Wicker, said in a statement that Wicker will also run for re-election next year.|url=https://www.djournal.com/news/state-news/army-veteran-ty-pinkins-announces-campaign-against-us-sen-roger-wicker/article_c32434ae-90e1-566c-955b-73c31792f699.html|access-date=January 3, 2023|website=Daily Journal|language=en-US|archive-date=January 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230104212536/https://www.djournal.com/news/state-news/army-veteran-ty-pinkins-announces-campaign-against-us-sen-roger-wicker/article_c32434ae-90e1-566c-955b-73c31792f699.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

